==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|fi|gmq-osw|siel}}, {{m|gmq-osw|siäl||soul}} (compare modern {{cog|sv|själ}}, {{cog|de|Seele}}, {{cog|en|soul}}), from {{der|fi|osx|sēola}}, ultimately from {{der|fi|gem-pro|*saiwalō}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[soul]]
# [[moving spirit]] {{gloss|one who provides significant impetus or guidance in a given venture, movement, enterprise etc.}}
# [[core]] of a [[valve]]

